<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/ai/pairing',
        '/components/chat',
        '/hooks/on-pairing',
        '/cli/bridge',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/assistant/lib/ClaudeCodeChat.test.ts',
            from: ["test('unpaired: the command and the click, and no chat yet'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/assistant/lib/ClaudeCodeChat.test.ts',
            from: ["test('paired: the chat, and the tools it cannot use'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/assistant/lib/Pairing.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a connection that takes too long offers to try again, and trying again asks again'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/assistant/lib/Pairing.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a visitor offline is told so, and the step returns once they are back'",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Show the chat once the visitor's Claude Code is paired">
        <p>Until the bridge pairs, <code>Pairing</code> offers a click and the terminal command
            that pair it. Once paired, it renders its children, beside a Reconnect.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import Chat from '@abide/abide/Chat.abide'
            import Pairing from '@abide/abide/Pairing.abide'
            import askClaudeCode from '../askClaudeCode.handler.ts'
            import permitClaudeCode from '../permitClaudeCode.handler.ts'
            </script>

            <Pairing>
                <Chat ask={askClaudeCode} permit={permitClaudeCode} />
            </Pairing>
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Offer a retry when connecting takes too long">
        <p>After <code>slowAfter</code> milliseconds of connecting, the step is
            <code>slow</code> and a Try again button reads the pairing again. A visitor with no
            network sees the <code>offline</code> step until they are back.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <Pairing slowAfter={5000}>…</Pairing>
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Say each step in the app's own words">
        <p>A <code>Message</code> component renders each step's message, handed the
            <code>step</code>.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <Pairing>
                {#component Message({ step }: { step: string })}
                    {step === 'click' ? 'Connect your Claude Code to the CRM.' : step}
                {/component}
                …
            </Pairing>
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Style each step of pairing">
        <p>The root carries <code>data-step</code>: <code>connecting</code>,
            <code>slow</code>, <code>offline</code>, <code>click</code>, <code>waiting</code>,
            <code>install</code>, <code>paired</code> or <code>unavailable</code>. Inside are the
            <code>message</code>, <code>command</code>, <code>copy</code>, <code>pair</code>,
            <code>retry</code> and <code>missing</code> parts.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import Pairing from '@abide/abide/Pairing.abide'
            </script>

            <Pairing
                class="flex flex-col gap-2 [&_[data-pairing=command]]:font-mono
                data-[step=waiting]:opacity-70"
            >
                …
            </Pairing>
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
